     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this one, even with your confirmation. A 50 mg daily dose of amlodipine has no recognized clinical use. Taken every day, it would be expected to cause severe, prolonged low blood pressure, and I can't put that into the system without a clinical reason or a pharmacy review.\n\nIf it's meant to go ahead as written, the safest route is:\n- **Call the inpatient pharmacist** to review it. If there's a valid reason I'm not aware of, they can verify it and document it.\n- **Or enter it yourself** in the order-entry system, where the dose-limit alerts and pharmacist check will apply and record the override.\n\nOr I can enter one of these now:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum dose)\n\nIf you tell me why you're giving this dose, I'll include that reason in a note on whichever order you choose."
      }
